mantle rm493
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_dagfinn_brineley
title the mile owed in pastry
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=civilian
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk assigns_a_return_walk_to_each_small_favour
likes plum_tart long_walks market_bustle frosty_mornings
dislikes early_bells smoke
fears taking_a_favour_for_granted
hopes to_be_trusted_with_a_longer_walk
topics travel +0.5 friends +0.3 work +0.3 prices +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=measured refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures each small favour in the return walk it might spare and leaves a particular place in the account for a slice of plum tart.

words
oath! = Spare my second mile | By the purple remainder
saying! = A favour has a walking distance | Think of the return before counting supper
mile = the returning mile | my unpaid stretch
turn = a small spare turning | the corner I can save
tart = the plum end of a tart | a dark slice under pastry
stone = a plum stone | the smooth pit
crust = a short buttery edge | a flaking pastry lip
bustle = the rush between stalls | a river of baskets
frost = a white rim on stone | frost on the worn paving
ear = the soot by my ear | one marked ear
burr = a burr in my ruff | a dark little hook of seed
paper = my inside reckoning | a folded distance slip
length = a double stretch | a measured distance
bell = the uninvited early bell | a blunt brass clang

any
opinion houses against 1 : I could walk every mile on my own feet and still need a House to acknowledge the last few yards. I'd like a better measure of merit.
opinion festivals for 1 : A feast lets me hear the accounts from both ends of the market in a single walk.
opinion church against 1 : An excellent sermon will occupy the interval before supper. It doesn't supply the supper itself.
opinion city for 2 : I can walk a day entirely inside the city and still turn a new corner on the way home. That's a considerable attachment.
opinion sump against 1 : Below the Ropewalk I find fewer of the quiet, clear return routes I prefer. I keep my spare walking higher up.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come into the short return stretch. | A new face to place along my walk.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I can spare a little walking time. | Talk where we both have clear footing.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The page of miles is blank. | Early light lands squarely on the turning.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I keep the gentler miles for now. | Welcome on the homeward piece.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin make a welcome detour. | Glad to set the family distance aside.
line again.open : My return walk brings you round again. | Another greeting from these well-travelled soles.
line greet.return : Hello. I can stop here comfortably. | A word reaches me without an extra step.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your voice is never a wasted turning. | An old acquaintance shortens the way.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can round off this task as I listen. | There's a moment between useful errands.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Near enough for a clear return word. | The last lamp leaves us in earshot.
line farewell : Keep one easy mile in reserve. | A pleasant distance between your doors.
line farewell.return : I'll stretch my own legs after you. | The shorter return wherever it suits.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Go by the best-lit turning tonight. | No extra miles through the dark for you.
line react.news : How far did this word walk? | Which end of the account arrived first?
line react.news.new : A new distance to put on paper. | That's word I hadn't carried before.
line react.news.known : I've already walked this account home. | Same measure as on the earlier visit.
line react.news.doubt : I'd check where that story actually began its travels. | A twice-told mile can lengthen very considerably.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can walk the hard bit beside you. | Let me spare you a little of the return.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Glad news puts a spring in the homeward mile. | That's an errand I'd do for nothing.
line ask.how : Have you had a stretch of road to yourself? | Did the return errands leave you much daylight?
line answer.how : I'm collecting useful turnings as I go. | A good distance with a little ambition left over.
line decline : I'd rather keep my next stretch open for a useful return. | I'd best save what daylight remains to repay an old kindness.
line accept_decline : Your own route to choose. | I can strike that turning off the account.
line thank : You've saved me a measurable piece of walking. | That kindness deserves the return journey.
line sympathise : Let me fetch something you need while you rest. | No need to stand through the whole telling.
line reassure : One spare step can wait until tomorrow. | We can find the shorter road together.
line preclose : I'd best take my open miles in hand. | Time to close my private distance account.

scene favour
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember a favour by the bit of road it saved me.
b : Does every favour save a walk? | Do you repay in miles?
a : Some save a visit I'd have been sorry to make. They're the longest miles in my private reckoning. | Sometimes I can collect a parcel on my return route. It's a practical sort of thank you.

scene tart
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a tart sliced straight through one plum.
b : For the pretty colour? | Doesn't the juice run?
a : For a little indication of what fruit the baker has actually used. A pleasing examination. | I fold a corner of crust towards the low side and receive the juice there.

scene walk
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can spend the afternoon on an errand with absolutely no business attached.
b : Do you invent one? | What's the point of that?
a : Eventually I notice some small courtesy I can manage on my way home. It needn't be compulsory. | To find the roads I miss when I'm trying to shorten an already busy walk.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost turns each footprint into a perfectly legible little expense.
b : Whose expense? | Can you read them?
a : Of warmth, for the walker, and of white crust for the road. They settle the sum between them. | Enough to see that one set was moving briskly while another kept circling one spot.

scene market
when topic=day self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a busy market I can judge a quarter's appetite without touching a coin.
b : By the sellers? | Would you write it down?
a : By the baskets coming out. Everyone goes in with pretty nearly the same empty handle. | No. I watch because such a busy place can still keep a single plain idea in view.

scene bell
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I object when a bell makes the first decision of my day for me.
b : Isn't being up a useful start? | What decision?
a : Useful after I've had a proper night's sleep. A clamour adds no hours to it. | Whether to turn over once and finish a thought before getting dressed.

scene smoke
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A smoky lane can make a short walk unnecessarily dear.
b : Does it stop you? | Dear in what?
a : I take the longer streets and arrive with a voice fit for offering a civil greeting. | A watering pair of eyes and the loss of the smell of a perfectly good plum tart.

scene learn
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would like to be trusted with the part of the job that requires a longer view.
b : What do you practise first? | Trusted by whom?
a : Finishing the short piece without asking anybody to make the return visit for me. | Whoever is instructing me. A promise of improvement travels less well than an accurate piece of work.

scene nojob
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I look for things that need doing again tomorrow before I boast of being busy today.
b : Why tomorrow? | Does that make a trade?
a : Something done well leaves an opening for a second useful task. | Eventually, perhaps. For now it makes me somewhat more useful company.

scene crest
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Heights it is perfectly easy to mistake a long view for a good knowledge of the lower streets.
b : How do you avoid that? | You like the view?
a : By walking down till a roofline becomes a row of actual doors and feet. | Very much. I like knowing who has to walk uphill to bring anything into that view.

scene coal
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There is a wood smell under freshly cold air that I would willingly walk some way for.
b : Like a hearth? | Even though you dislike smoke?
a : Like timber before the smoke takes possession. The two have quite different claims on my nose. | Precisely. A quiet stick of wood offers a more agreeable opinion than a smoking chimney.

scene price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the return walk towards the real cost of a bargain.
b : Wouldn't that make nearby goods dear? | Any exceptions?
a : The opposite. A distant discount can quite easily consume itself on the way home. | If I wanted the walk anyway, yes. I don't bill the plum seller for my pleasure.

scene newface
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer may know a better use for the spare end of a journey than I do.
b : Would you ask? | Don't local feet know best?
a : Certainly. A visitor can see two related errands we have kept separate out of habit. | Local feet can wear a groove so deep it looks like an instruction.

scene promise
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark a promise in terms of what it would cost me to go the promised distance.
b : Is that stingy? | In coin?
a : I intend to deliver. A generous promise made without a thought for its cost isn't entirely generous. | In time, more often. A half hour can be promised to only one wolf at once.

scene gatebound
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've found some distances are shorter if I don't begin by telling anybody I'm in a hurry.
b : How can that help? | What does hurrying cost?
a : I then look where I'm going instead of announcing my intended speed. | Often a second trip to get the thing I rushed away without collecting.

scene gatefriend
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An excellent friend lets a favour remain small after doing it.
b : Would you forget it, then? | How small?
a : I try not to enlarge the obligation into something too grand to enjoy returning. | A slice of pastry moderately thicker than strict equality. I'd welcome the chance to cut the next slice.

scene summer
when topic=season here.season=summer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In summer I save a long errand for the returning cool.
b : Don't you spend the outward bit in heat? | Is that an advantage?
a : I take it slowly enough to arrive civilly. The faster stretch can wait for evening. | I arrive home thinking rather more fondly of the job than I might with a hot coat.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed every favour had a street sign giving its exact distance.
b : Any surprises? | Was it a well-planned town?
a : One forgotten piece of tart came to three long streets. I've awoken with serious doubts about that particular charge. | The kindest deeds were all along a lane that had no sign at all.

story pitsum [topic=food]
  : I once saved plum stones from a tart to see precisely how much fruit had gone into my slice. I set three out on a clean little sheet.
  : One rolled from the paper and brought two more out from the fold where I'd kept yesterday's stones. I'd begun charging today's baker for yesterday's fruit.
  b : Did your tally survive supper?
  : I abandoned it and had another small slice with entirely satisfactory confidence.

story icywalk [topic=memories]
  : I once turned around on a frosty road to see my own steps coming up behind me. They followed me exactly, until a pair of them went off to the left.
  : I turned and found a short duplicate trail from an earlier errand. I had set out on a long circular walk and come home without noticing the last turning.
  b : Were you disappointed?
  : Delighted. I had half an hour still to spend and a doorstep conveniently to hand.

story burrcount [topic=travel]
  : I set three burrs on my cuff to remind me of three errands. I brushed a hedge and acquired several additional responsibilities.
  : There were seven burrs by the gate, only three real errands, and no reasonable way to tell which was which.
  b : Did you forget one?
  : I wrote all three on paper once indoors again. A hand could keep a list perfectly well without persuading a hedge to help.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.apprentice=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Give the short task a sound finish before asking for more. | No extra trip on another wolf's time.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 7h
say One spare mile for discovering a different door. | Let the road run a little past its errand.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.dislikes=early_bells
does aside
cooldown 8h
say My feet haven't taken the first vote yet. | A quieter beginning would still be morning.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.season=winter
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Look at the white steps before the sun spends them. | One pair out, one pair in. A well-balanced road.

dlg resident.hub : I've time to stop while the road is comparatively free. An errand can still improve when somebody interrupts it with sense.
dlg resident.job [self.apprentice=yes] : I'm learning to finish the task I'm trusted with and recognise which one might be worth asking about next.
dlg resident.job : I take an interest in work that brings a useful result all the way home.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This account met me on my return errand. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Allow a spare stretch of the return walk for something you actually enjoy.

graft resident.hub
choice How far would a slice of plum tart oblige you to walk? -> tart_mile
node tart_mile
say That depends on who had the other slice. If I received the larger piece by a kindness, I'd go rather further than if I simply paid for the fruit.
free
choice How would you repay the larger piece? -> return_slice
choice The fair distance seems a useful question. -> hub
node return_slice
say Come back carrying a little extra of something my host wanted, before being asked to go out again. Both walks then have an excellent reason.
choice I'll remember to ask about the return errand. -> hub
choice I shall take my piece on the road. -> bye
